{"tool_name":"mocha","contents":["oeb","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"MoChA","home":"https://github.com/freeseek/mocha","summary":"CLONAL HEMATOPOIESIS IN A CENTENARIAN COHORT.\n\nMOsaic CHromosomal Alterations (MoChA) caller.\n\nA bcftools extension to call mosaic chromosomal alterations starting from phased VCF files with either B Allele Frequency (BAF) and Log R Ratio (LRR) or allelic depth (AD). If you use this tool in your publication, please cite the following paper and preprint:.\n\nThis command will create a list of variants falling within segmental duplications with low divergence (<2%), high levels of missingness (>2%), variants with excess heterozygosity (p<1e-6), and variants that correlate with sex in an unexpected way (p<1e-6).","addition_date":"2020-01-14T09:36:35Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:51:52.101769Z","tool_type":["Library"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:MoChA","edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Genotyping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3196"},{"term":"Phasing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3454"},{"term":"Variant calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227"}]}],"name":"MoChA","owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"pmcid":"PMC6846495"}],"topic":[{"term":"DNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0654"},{"term":"Genetic variation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0199"},{"term":"Genotype and phenotype","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0625"},{"term":"Geriatric medicine","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3399"},{"term":"Microarray experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3518"}],"validated":1},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:mocha/lib/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpret